% n13: applying a NON-FUNCTION. `a : A` applied to `b : A`.
% Added because mutation testing showed that removing the "head must be a pi"
% check broke nothing in the corpus -- every existing application test had a
% well-typed function at the head, so the check was untested.
1 sort 0
axiom A : 1
2 const A
axiom a : 2
3 const A
axiom b : 3
4 const a
5 const b
6 app 4 5
7 const A
check 6 : 7
